{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "8bf9a286-00f8-4428-b046-8c92608a8cb9"/*CurvesToGeometryExp*/,
  "Description": "Fills closed curves into solid geometry and optionally extrudes them with a bevel - the way from [TextToCurves] to solid 3D text. The result is CPU geometry, so put [GeometryToMesh] after it to draw it.\n\nDepth 0 gives a flat fill; with Depth, front and back caps are joined by walls, and Bevel rounds (or with BevelSegments 1 chamfers) the edges. Overlapping and nested contours are resolved by the fill rule (non-zero by default, EvenOdd as option), so variable-font overlaps disappear. One mesh part per curve part (glyph), with the curve's part attributes carried over for [ColorFacesFromAttribute] and [GeometryToMeshChunks]; the face attribute IsSide marks walls and bevels. Walls and bevels are smooth shaded along round outlines and hard at corners sharper than SmoothAngle; FlatShading makes every wall and bevel facet flat. Weight offsets the outline outwards (negative: inwards) for a faux bold or light look; it thickens stems and shrinks counters, so it stays convincing only for small amounts. Tolerance is the flattening precision. Keep Bevel below half of the thinnest stroke: a larger bevel folds the inset outline over itself and opens the surface.\n\nAKA: extrude text, 3d text, fill curves, tessellate, curves to mesh",
  "InputUis": [
    {
      "InputId": "3d7b7c7a-8e11-4b9a-8b7e-3e8a4a6f2b91"/*SideLoops*/,
      "Position": {
